WEBVTT

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.440
Brother, I mean, Seiran.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:39.950
It says that in Shuurei's report as well,  but who is this man called Tan-tan?

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.740
Tan-tan-kun?

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:48.710
Tan-tan-kun's real name is Shin Suou, and he's a foolish raccoon.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:51.340
A-A foolish raccoon?

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.220
You're Kou Shuurei, right?

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:03.220
Well, yes, I am.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:08.100
I was kinda told to take my best shot and propose marriage to you.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.560
Huh?

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:11.110
A raccoon?

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.070
Here.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.160
What?

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:15.670
Well then.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:16.450
What?

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:29.420
Why on earth was that person holding a golden raccoon?

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.570
Who cares?

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.220
Why are you upset?

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.710
I'm not upset.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.490
Hey, you! What are you doing down there, spacing out?!

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.140
Whoa! He's been swept away!

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.610
That's quite foolish, I agree.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.280
He's a fool, but he's not just a fool.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:04.380
He's a fool who can be useful because of his foolishness.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:10.120
As it says in the report, he helped a lot in the counterfeiting and forgery case.

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:12.100
Right...

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:18.990
A bamboo shoot?

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.970
Tan-tan-kun...

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.470
Tan-tan?

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:26.390
Tan-tan-kun of the Tan-tan-tanuki.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:34.120
The woman named Karin seems to be visiting each and every shop that sells paintings.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.350
The painting and calligraphic art stores.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.850
Those stores?

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:45.170
When she finds a forgery, she points it out and goes dashing off to the next store.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.140
Get out of my way, you bastards over there!

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:51.320
You're in my way!

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.710
Oh? Hey hottie! Where ya goin'?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.160
Get lost!

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:12.230
It's a bit odd.

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:16.180
In order to convince customers that the forgeries are the originals,

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:19.140
there's a condition that has to be fulfilled, isn't there?

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:20.510
A condition?

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:23.240
That's right. They mustn't be found.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:25.860
Oh, the originals?

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:31.830
If the whereabouts of the originals were known,
any attempt to sell a fake would be discovered quickly.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:35.300
So the whereabouts of the originals has to remain unknown.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:42.270
In that case, the mysterious art dealer
who's selling the fakes has the originals.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:46.010
Indeed. Tan-tan, you're smart.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:50.660
The mysterious art dealer buys the original artworks from the rich and the nobility,

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.720
creates forgeries of them,

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.700
and sells them as the originals.

00:04:54.700 --> 00:05:01.530
In addition, if you pay for the originals with counterfeit coins, you earn twice as much.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:07.700
If you're gonna do it, then it's better to do as much as you can.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.740
Originally, I visited the town for...

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:12.940
You know...

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:13.870
What?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:15.870
Ouch!

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.660
Did you really mean that just now?

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:19.400
Huh?

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:23.370
That bit about "it's better to do as much as you can."

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:26.730
It kinda sounded like you were saying that to yourself.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.870
Why do you try so hard?

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:34.140
In any case, the Imperial Court will run just fine with or without you.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:40.140
If you're there, they'll use you when it's convenient; but if you're not, they won't be concerned.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.400
You're on your own now, right?

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:46.080
What's in it for you to work so hard?

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.750
You finally have free time. Why don't you just take it easy?

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.670
I don't understand you.

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:52.850
Tan-tan?

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:53.370
What?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.160
You better hold yourself for a second.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.150
What?

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:07.090
Ouch!

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.090
What did you do that for?!

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.330
Shut up!

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:14.210
There are times you can't get through unless you pretend to be strong!

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.930
For those I want to impress, I'll pretend I'm strong!

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.750
For those whose approval I need, I won't whine!

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:24.400
Even so, there's no way everything in this world will work out!

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.900
So there were times I was glad I worked hard!

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.780
There were times I was glad I worked hard.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.910
That's why I pretend to be strong.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.960
They're all fakes.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:36.410
I thought so.

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:38.250
You'd...

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:41.490
better stay out of this from now on.

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:44.700
If a government official is behind this,

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.960
then the Section of Government Inspection is probably involved already.

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:49.460
The Section of Government Inspection...

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.250
They investigate official corruption

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.680
and can even take measures against officials independently.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.480
If you continue to involve yourself, you'll be exceeding your authority.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.730
Huh? Why are you in the garden?

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.730
Tan-tan! What are you doing here?

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:14.680
You try way too hard, and you're really too good.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:17.040
You just get on my nerves.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:21.040
Staying with you feels exhausting.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:26.850
You must truly believe in your sense of justice and all sorts of other nice stuff too.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:31.050
I thought, how sickening is that?

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.380
I don't know if...

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:40.080
what you say is true, but I don't think society will go easy on you.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:46.060
Then again, you never said "Why don't you try harder?" to me, did you?

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:48.740
D-Didn't I?

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.070
No.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.450
That's the only thing that gave me pause.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:58.640
If you'd said that, even just once, I suppose even a calm guy like me would've been annoyed.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.020
Is that so?

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:04.310
But you didn't, so I'll show you my gratitude for that.

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:06.330
Huh? Show your gratitude?

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:15.590
Stop! Stop!

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.570
What's wrong with this wall?!

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:24.520
How dare it obstruct me?!

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.800
It's exceedingly insulting!

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:27.900
I will never forgive this!

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:29.400
No!

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.040
What's going on?!

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:33.000
What are these dowdy men doing here?! Three of them!

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.570
I can't stand this! Shoo! Get lost!

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.450
Why... are you here?

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.590
What's this gathering about?

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:54.590
If you've got business with our family, the entrance gate is over there.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:58.350
What? This is your home?

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:01.680
Banri!

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:07.640
Mother...

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:08.790
Mother!

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:11.150
Mother!

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.200
Mother...

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:13.950
Banri...

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:14.850
Mother...

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:21.900
All these... Don't tell me that little child painted them all?

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:24.160
What an incredible talent.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:34.880
This is...

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.610
A mold for counterfeit coins.

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:43.140
Banri, don't tell me you carved this, too?

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:49.190
Y-Yeah. They suggested I try carving for a change.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.210
They took the best one away, though.

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:53.610
I don't believe this.

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:58.570
Uh, why are you people trespassing in my house?!

00:09:58.570 --> 00:09:59.640
Oh, Dad.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.200
S-S-Suou,

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.400
what's going on?

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:05.570
Dad, your humble moneymaking venture's been revealed, that's what's going on.

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:06.450
What?

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:12.460
This means that Tan-tan's father is the cause of all...

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.770
You were the one who said,

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:17.930
"The person with the original is the most likely suspect."

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:22.880
If you write up this case in detail, instead of just filing a report, and present it to the Imperial Court,

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:26.220
your suspension might be lifted sooner.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:30.720
I see. This Tan-tan fellow seems to be quite useful.

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.210
I'm impressed that you ended the case

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:37.950
by minting new coins from Karen's, I mean, Heki Yuukoku's successful design,

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:39.330
at the end of all this.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:41.750
However...

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:42.350
What?

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:47.580
A similar incident occurred right after that case.

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:03.570
As part of a reorganization of ranks and personnel,

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:09.560
those joukan listed to the right, who are not currently employed, will be dismissed in a month's time.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.190
See?

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:13.570
Life's not that easy.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.250
Just forget about them.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:29.520
It's not like you're their guardian or supervisor, are you?

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:31.280
I agree.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:34.650
Well, umm...

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:37.380
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.880
I'm Riku Seiga.

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:41.880
R-Right...

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:45.160
I don't think you should worry about them.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:49.810
They're all quite well off at home.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:53.980
So, do you think you can sort yourself out somehow?

00:11:54.250 --> 00:12:00.150
Sure, my supervisor only made me a joukan temporarily because of circumstances at work.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:01.990
Really?

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:04.110
The problem here is...

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:08.560
You don't have time for them.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:14.830
Of course, I'll take care of myself, but if I can do something for them in passing, then I want to try.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.590
Stand up!

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:27.470
This is not your home or playground! It's your workplace!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:31.520
At the end of the day, whether or not you get fired is up to you!

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:34.810
If you don't want to be fired, grab a job yourself!

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.330
The price has gone up again.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.420
Yes, Shuurei-chan.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:48.270
But rather than saying, "It's gone up,"
it'd be more appropriate to say, "It had to go up."

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:50.050
What do you mean by that?

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:56.030
I thought you would've noticed, but there's quite a lot of white sand mixed in, right?

00:12:56.030 --> 00:12:56.920
Yes.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.520
That's when this came in handy.

00:12:58.520 --> 00:12:59.420
What?

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:01.310
You pour the salt in here.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.120
This way, a lot of impurities can be removed.

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.810
The local guild provided them for us quickly.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:23.400
However, the guild apparently doesn't know where the sand was added to the salt.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:28.220
Are you saying... the salt is being intercepted somewhere?

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:29.770
It's such a nuisance.

00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:32.220
Hey, what are you doing here?

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:33.340
Tan-tan...

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:39.030
This is a serious threat.

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:39.730
What?

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:44.170
Salt is essential for life.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:47.410
People can't live without salt.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:49.430
Well... yeah...

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:55.070
Rising salt prices are alarming, if you take a long term view.

00:13:55.070 --> 00:14:00.540
More importantly, aren't you supposed to be thinking about how to avoid dismissal?

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:01.980
There!

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:04.620
If I find out where the sand is being added to the salt,

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:08.600
understand the situation, and prevent salt price inflation,

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:11.460
then that should suffice to avoid getting fired.

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:14.620
What a coincidence.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:15.870
Seiga-san.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:21.130
You two must be really close if you're together on a day off.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:22.460
It's not like that.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.990
I only ran into Tan-tan by chance. I'm just doing a bit of research.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:27.470
Research?

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.090
I've got time.

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:31.340
I'd like to hear about it, if you don't mind.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:45.020
The family that's been attempting to buy saltworks in Ranshuu...

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.030
is the Chin family.

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:52.530
The Chin family wouldn't tamper with salt from Ranshuu,

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:56.190
perhaps because they planned to purchase saltworks there.

00:14:56.190 --> 00:15:01.060
I heard that the mistress has been spending a lot more on clothes and accessories lately.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:06.300
The husband seems to be living it up in the flower district too.

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:08.550
There's no doubt.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:12.050
Yes... but I feel...

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:17.200
You're right, it's odd that they're spending money so carelessly.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:21.020
The cost of purchasing saltworks is too great to believe they're relying

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.820
only on the profit from salt.

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:26.570
A recent case where a large sum of money went missing...

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:30.180
It can't be!

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:36.410
Please.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:40.340
What beautiful jade and pearls...

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:42.730
Put it on the shelf over there.

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:43.600
Yes, mistress.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:51.810
Wow, it's full of expensive jewels.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:04.020
The report and the evidence haven't been submitted, yet...

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.060
Hey, I thought you'd come.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:06.980
Oh,

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:08.360
Seiga-san!

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:13.910
You're hopelessly soft-hearted, aren't you?

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.200
Seiga-san...

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:22.320
Honestly, the last month has been nothing but a pain.

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:27.030
If you'd interfered again, you'd have ruined my reputation.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:31.710
I thought I was going to explode in anger with you over the forgery and counterfeiting case.

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.600
Then...

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.720
you took the report!

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:42.490
I submitted the report and the evidence ages ago.

00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:44.440
You're through.

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:47.440
I don't think so.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:48.770
Tan-tan!

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:50.760
Why are you here?

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:56.240
Hey, didn't you say that this was my mother's residence, Seiga?

00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:59.240
I'd heard rumors about you.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:02.530
That you were the youngest undercover inspector ever appointed.

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:09.790
Remember the actual seal that was used to counterfeit money?

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:11.540
That's right...

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:15.680
We never found the seal that was actually used for counterfeiting.

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:18.430
That's why I've been looking for it all this time.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:22.120
If I found the seal, then it would prove that the true culprit was someone else,

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:24.640
and my dad's death sentence would be lifted.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:33.770
Here comes the Director General of the Section of Government Inspection.

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:34.610
What?

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:39.240
So you were a soft-hearted fool
through and through, Kou Shuurei.

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:41.620
You're utterly useless!

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:43.240
However,

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:46.700
you have a quick mind, probably as good as Seiga's.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:51.630
Don't expect that you'll get away with your soft-hearted foolishness in my section.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:54.850
If you're prepared to take on anything, then come.

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:58.530
All in all, Shuurei did well.

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:01.090
She rescued the Imperial Court.

00:18:01.090 --> 00:18:03.350
Yes, I think so too.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.520
But... Shuurei's joining the Section of Government Inspection, isn't she?

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:10.980
She'll be busy. I wonder if I'll see her?

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:13.520
And the next head of the Riku family?

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:16.650
I hear that Seiga has a quick mind.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.820
What if Shuurei falls for him?

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:23.790
Indeed, oujo-sama is acting very friendly to him.

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:26.870
What?!

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:31.090
Come to think of it, where's Kouyuu these days?

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:33.490
I called him because I wanted to talk to him about something.

00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:37.460
As usual, Kouyuu-dono must be lost somewhere.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:40.300
Lost, huh? Just like always.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:41.850
How could it be...

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:45.810
Why does it take half a day to get here from the Civil Service ministry?!

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:47.410
Where are you, demon of time?!

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.190
Come out! Show yourself!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.310
Come out, I said!

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:53.400
Curse you, you coward!

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:57.690
Kouyuu, I wanted to talk to you about something.

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:01.700
Talk to me? I'm busy right now. Make it quick.

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:05.700
I am... considering taking a wife.

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:09.230
What changed your mind?

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:14.830
However, among the common people, a husband has just one wife.

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:18.970
I think I will follow their style and be monogamous.

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:23.470
In other words, I will take only one wife!

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:29.960
Well, I think that's good.

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:33.480
I'll work to make sure the proposal passes at the next Imperial Conference.

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:36.450
I'm going. I have work to do.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:41.910
He must've made this decision with the intention of marrying oujo-sama,

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.490
but I hope it doesn't backfire on him.

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:51.500
I wonder how Shuuei is doing.

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:58.150
If you're asking about that man, he must be lost and confused even as we speak.

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:05.760
Kouyuu's lost his way and... probably so has Shuuei.

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:22.780
His Highness presented me with an iris crest.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:27.290
A person only receives this symbol if he pledges absolute loyalty to the Emperor.

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:46.180
In terms of age, I'm the eldest, followed by Kouyuu, then Your Highness, I suppose.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:49.360
No, I'm the middle.

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:53.010
From the top: Shuuei, me, then Kouyuu.

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:58.950
Hey, you ate me head first?

00:20:58.950 --> 00:21:03.650
I'm going to play hard against you, so I'm provoking you first.

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:07.660
I-I lost...

00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:13.140
I became quite serious about this game.

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:16.480
Ah!

00:21:16.930 --> 00:21:22.360
Your Highness, please don't eat just the top dumplings because you lost the game.

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:24.860
You're giving me a sly hint, aren't you?

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:32.570
What is it?

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:34.350
Your Highness.

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:37.110
No, I know.

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:38.360
A holiday, right?

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:41.000
I lost. There's nothing I can do.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.720
It's only for a short while, remember.

00:21:46.100 --> 00:21:48.790
Yes, I'll take a short one.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:50.340
Hold on.

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:53.490
If you don't mind, will you eat it as is?

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:56.120
Oh? Sure.

00:22:04.970 --> 00:22:10.500
I wonder why His Highness presented iris crests to Kouyuu and me.

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:11.300
What?

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:15.270
Was it because only Kouyuu and I were there at the time?

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:17.140
I think so.

00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:24.960
I think that at the time, only Ran-shogun and Kouyuu-sama were worthy to receive irises.

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:27.200
Why is that?

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:31.400
You'll have to ask Ryuuki himself for the answer.

00:22:33.770 --> 00:22:34.930
That's true.

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:42.350
But brother... Seiran, you're too hard on Shuuei, don't you think?

00:22:42.350 --> 00:22:45.250
Ryuuki-sama, you're too soft on them.

00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:47.360
You've presented them iris crests,

00:22:47.360 --> 00:22:51.250
but both Kouyuu-dono and Ran-shogun are frequently absent from your side.

00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:54.270
Even so, you put your highest trust in the Kou and Ran families.

00:22:54.900 --> 00:22:58.640
Perhaps the other nobles are dissatisfied by that.

00:22:59.430 --> 00:23:02.700
Why won't you trust us more?

00:23:02.700 --> 00:23:06.180
In the worst case, you'll be isolated.

00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:11.280
By the time you come to regret it, it will be too late.

00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:20.480
I am the Emperor of Saiunkoku.

00:23:21.330 --> 00:23:23.920
To be an Emperor... is painful.

00:24:45.120 --> 00:24:46.250
That bastard Seiga!

00:24:46.500 --> 00:24:49.650
He'd better stop giving himself airs! The cynical swine! The evil rascal!

00:24:51.760 --> 00:24:55.630
What? Oh no, I was just joking. It's just a j-o-k-e!
